  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.form1040-line2b",
  "notes": "Computes Form 1040 line 2b from the exact seven-family positive-interest composition less four separately closed adjustment classes: the three Schedule B classes carried forward from v4, plus the canonical obligation-acquisition accrued-interest class. The fourth class differs in kind from the other three: it is derived by an adopted rule from ordinary facts the person supplied about a purchase, rather than contributed as an adjustment amount, and it publishes nothing unless each acquisition resolved against exactly one recorded Form 1099-INT box-1 item. The existing subtract vocabulary is used; the comparison guard refuses to publish a negative taxable-interest result when adjustments exceed the positive basis.",
